    {
      "id": "intro_4",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "Does the writer think the parents were lucky or unlucky to gain prosperity in this way? Why?",
      "translation": "作者认为父母以这种方式获得富强是幸运还是不幸？为什么？",
      "startTime": 9.99,
      "endTime": 20.21,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "prosperity",
            "pos": "n.",
            "meaning": "繁荣，昌盛"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "intro_5",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "In democratic countries any efforts to restrict the freedom of the press are rightly condemned.",
      "translation": "在民主国家，任何限制新闻自由的努力都会受到理所当然的谴责。",
      "startTime": 20.22,
      "endTime": 28.58,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "democratic",
            "pos": "adj.",
            "meaning": "民主的"
          },
          {
            "word": "restrict",
            "pos": "v.",
            "meaning": "限制"
          },
          {
            "word": "condemned",
            "pos": "v.",
            "meaning": "谴责"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "However, this freedom can easily be abused.",
      "translation": "然而，这种自由很容易被滥用。",
      "startTime": 28.59,
      "endTime": 33.73,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "abused",
            "pos": "v.",
            "meaning": "滥用"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "Stories about people often attract far more public attention than political events.",
      "translation": "有关个人的故事往往比政治事件更能引起公众的关注。",
      "startTime": 33.74,
      "endTime": 40.72,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "political",
            "pos": "adj.",
            "meaning": "政治的"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "Though we may enjoy reading about the lives of others, it is extremely doubtful whether we would equally enjoy reading about ourselves.",
      "translation": "虽然我们可能喜欢阅读他人的生活，但非常令人怀疑我们是否同样喜欢阅读关于我们自己的报道。",
      "startTime": 40.73,
      "endTime": 51.75,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "doubtful",
            "pos": "adj.",
            "meaning": "怀疑的"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "Acting on the contention that facts are sacred, reporters can cause untold suffering to individuals by publishing details about their private lives.",
      "translation": "基于事实圣神不可侵犯的论点，记者可以通过发表个人私生活的细节给个人造成无法言喻的痛苦。",
      "startTime": 51.76,
      "endTime": 65.82,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "contention",
            "pos": "n.",
            "meaning": "论点"
          },
          {
            "word": "sacred",
            "pos": "adj.",
            "meaning": "神圣的"
          },
          {
            "word": "untold",
            "pos": "adj.",
            "meaning": "数不尽的，言语无法形容的"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "Newspapers exert such tremendous influence that they can not only bring about major changes to the lives of ordinary people but can even overthrow a government.",
      "translation": "报纸发挥着如此巨大的影响力，以至于它们不仅能给普通人的生活带来重大变化，甚至可以推翻一个政府。",
      "startTime": 65.83,
      "endTime": 79.21,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "exert",
            "pos": "v.",
            "meaning": "施加"
          },
          {
            "word": "tremendous",
            "pos": "adj.",
            "meaning": "巨大的"
          },
          {
            "word": "overthrow",
            "pos": "v.",
            "meaning": "推翻"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "The story of a poor family that acquired fame and fortune overnight, dramatically illustrates the power of the press.",
      "translation": "一个贫穷家庭一夜之间获得名利的经历，生动地说明了新闻界的力量。",
      "startTime": 79.22,
      "endTime": 88.29,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "fame",
            "pos": "n.",
            "meaning": "名声"
          },
          {
            "word": "fortune",
            "pos": "n.",
            "meaning": "财产，命运"
          },
          {
            "word": "dramatically",
            "pos": "adv.",
            "meaning": "戏剧性地"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "The family lived in Aberdeen, a small town of 23, 000 inhabitants in South Dakota.",
      "translation": "这家人住在阿伯丁，南达科他州一个拥有23,000名居民的小镇。",
      "startTime": 88.3,
      "endTime": 96.01,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "inhabitant",
            "pos": "n.",
            "meaning": "居民"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "As the parents had five children, life was a perpetual struggle against poverty.",
      "translation": "由于父母有5个孩子，生活就是一场与贫困的无休止的斗争。",
      "startTime": 96.02,
      "endTime": 102.11,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "perpetual",
            "pos": "adj.",
            "meaning": "永久的，不间断的"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s9",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "They were expecting their sixth child and were faced with even more pressing economic problems.",
      "translation": "他们正期待着第6个孩子，面临着更加紧迫的经济问题。",
      "startTime": 102.12,
      "endTime": 109.5,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "pressing",
            "pos": "adj.",
            "meaning": "紧迫的"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s10",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "If they had only had one more child, the fact would have passed unnoticed.",
      "translation": "如果他们只多了一个孩子，这个事实就会在不经意间过去。",
      "startTime": 109.51,
      "endTime": 115.52,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "unnoticed",
            "pos": "adj.",
            "meaning": "被忽视的"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s11",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "They would have continued to struggle against economic odds and would have lived in obscurity.",
      "translation": "他们本会继续在经济困境中挣扎，并在默默无闻中生活。",
      "startTime": 115.53,
      "endTime": 122.5,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "odds",
            "pos": "n.",
            "meaning": "不平等，机会"
          },
          {
            "word": "obscurity",
            "pos": "n.",
            "meaning": "默默无闻"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s12",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "But they suddenly became the parents of quintuplets, four girls and a boy, an event which radically changed their lives.",
      "translation": "但他们突然成了五胞胎的父母——4个女孩和1个男孩，这一事件彻底改变了他们的生活。",
      "startTime": 122.51,
      "endTime": 132.98,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "quintuplets",
            "pos": "n.",
            "meaning": "五胞胎"
